<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῠλαία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῠλᾱγορ-αίη</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύνοδος</span>), ἡ, fem.
		of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυλαῖος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>meeting of the Amphictyons at Pylae</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.213
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.10.2
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἠρινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					230.27
				</span></i>
			 (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐαρινή</span> Decr.Amphict. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.154
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπωρινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					239
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>C</u>
				32
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετοπωρινή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					9.3.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>right of sending deputies to the Amphictyonic Council</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.
				5.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>place where the Amphictyons met</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				2507.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2524.11
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.409a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>promiscuous crowd</i>, such as was found at these meetings:
			hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύθων ἀπιθάνων . . πυλαία</span>
			<i>farrago</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Art.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.924d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> a place
			(perh. in Arcadia, cf. <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>) considered undesirable for Spartan youths, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.239c
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
